\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x$ or any other non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ \n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x}{‖x‖\\,‖{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 3}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{36}\\sqrt{18}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{6\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." 13194139535638 true] [17592186358832 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358833 13194139535638 true] [17592186358832 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358834 13194139535638 true] [17592186358832 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358835 13194139535638 true] [17592186358832 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358836 13194139535638 true] [17592186358832 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358837 13194139535638 true] [17592186358832 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535638 true] [17592186358832 1041 "selection" 13194139535638 true] [17592186358832 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358833 13194139535638 true] [17592186358832 1110 #uuid "9b1d76bc-0f00-5a24-82fb-37502bab4aa6" 13194139535638 true] [17592186358833 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" 13194139535638 true] [17592186358833 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535638 true] [17592186358833 1111 #uuid "0b4b71f3-dc38-5620-9fce-87e